From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:39:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] sidebar: the row's Stop Generation asks first, as the panel's
 does

Operator, 2026-11-25, after the live test of 0.27.0: the Stop button on a
running thread's row in the sidebar stopped the turn at once, while the
agent panel's Stop Generation asked first (0166). The row went straight to
AgentPanel::cancel_thread, which calls ThreadView::cancel_generation and
skips the confirmation.

AgentPanel::confirm_cancel_thread finds the thread's view the same way and
calls ThreadView::confirm_cancel_generation instead, so every Stop the
operator starts goes through one prompt ("Stop generation?", Stop / Keep
Going). The sidebar's stop_thread takes the window for it. A thread with no
turn running stops without asking, as the panel's button already does.

The other cancel_thread caller in the sidebar, archiving a running thread,
is left alone: 0167 has already asked "Archive?" by then.

Tests (sidebar_stop_confirm_tests.rs): Keep Going leaves the turn running,
and nothing stops before the answer; Stop stops it.

In the claude-agent-acp-plus group, where 0166 and 0167 are, at its end.
---

diff --git a/crates/agent_ui/src/agent_panel.rs b/crates/agent_ui/src/agent_panel.rs
index f70b0a8..fcd7814 100644
--- a/crates/agent_ui/src/agent_panel.rs
+++ b/crates/agent_ui/src/agent_panel.rs
@@ -4922,6 +4922,32 @@ impl AgentPanel {
         false
     }
 
+    /// Stop Generation started outside the thread's own view -- the sidebar's row button
+    /// (operator, 2026-11-25) -- asks through the same confirmation as the view's own button
+    /// (0166's `ThreadView::confirm_cancel_generation`), so no surface stops a turn unasked.
+    /// Returns whether this panel holds the thread.
+    pub fn confirm_cancel_thread(
+        &self,
+        thread_id: &ThreadId,
+        window: &mut Window,
+        cx: &mut Context<Self>,
+    ) -> bool {
+        let conversation_views = self
+            .active_conversation_view()
+            .into_iter()
+            .chain(self.retained_threads.values());
+
+        for conversation_view in conversation_views {
+            if *thread_id == conversation_view.read(cx).thread_id {
+                if let Some(thread_view) = conversation_view.read(cx).root_thread_view() {
+                    thread_view.update(cx, |view, cx| view.confirm_cancel_generation(window, cx));
+                    return true;
+                }
+            }
+        }
+        false
+    }
+
     fn update_thread_work_dirs(&self, cx: &mut Context<Self>) {
         let new_work_dirs = self.project.read(cx).default_path_list(cx);
         let new_worktree_paths = self.project.read(cx).worktree_paths(cx);
